<article class="env-lemma" id="002N">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/002N">Lemma <span data-tag="002N">4.14.11</span>.</a> Let $M : \mathcal{I} \to \mathcal{C}$ be a diagram. Write $I = \mathop{\mathrm{Ob}}\nolimits (\mathcal{I})$ and $A = \text{Arrows}(\mathcal{I})$. Denote $s, t : A \to I$ the source and target maps. Suppose that $\prod _{i \in I} M_ i$ and $\prod _{a \in A} M_{t(a)}$ exist. Suppose that the equalizer of </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix{ \prod _{i \in I} M_ i \ar@<1ex>[r]^\phi \ar@<-1ex>[r]_\psi &  \prod _{a \in A} M_{t(a)} }  \]
</div>
  <p> exists, where the morphisms are determined by their components as follows: $p_ a \circ \psi = M(a) \circ p_{s(a)}$ and $p_ a \circ \phi = p_{t(a)}$. Then this equalizer is the limit of the diagram. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Omitted. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>